[center][size=6][b]KeeperSpawner[/b][/size]
A lightweight item spawner for Graveyard Keeper 2[/center]

Press [b]O[/b] (the letter) in game, find an item and click it to add it to your inventory.

[center][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3810736028]Steam Workshop[/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner]GitHub (source code)[/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner/releases]GitHub releases[/url][/center]

[b]New in 1.1.0:[/b] KeeperSpawner shows up in the game's [b]Mods[/b] menu when [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] is installed, with its status and settings. The Framework is optional; KeeperSpawner still works without it.

[line]
[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]All 726 regular items with the game's own icons, names in your game language and bronze / silver / gold quality stars
[*]15 categories: building, food, farming, alchemy, potions, tools, equipment, fishing, body parts, graves, church, papers, bags, quest, other
[*]Search by name or id, accent-insensitive
[*]Quality filter, grid or list view
[*]Click adds 1, 10 or a full stack; Shift+Click adds 1; the info panel adds any amount from 1 to 999
[*]Favorites (right-click) and the last 5 added items
[*]Quest items hidden by default, so you do not break quests by accident
[*]UI in all 17 languages of the game
[*]Optional [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] support: see the mod and change its settings from Mods in the main menu or pause menu
[*]Switches itself off with a log message, instead of breaking the game, if a game update changes the code it relies on
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5]BepInEx 5.4.23.5 (win_x64)[/url]
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] 0.1.19 or newer, for the in-game Mods menu
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx: extract [i]BepInEx_win_x64_5.4.23.5.zip[/i] next to [i]GraveyardKeeper2.exe[/i], start the game once and close it.
[*]Extract [i]KeeperSpawner-1.1.0.zip[/i] into the game folder, so that you get
[code]Graveyard Keeper 2\BepInEx\plugins\KeeperSpawner\KeeperSpawner.dll
Graveyard Keeper 2\BepInEx\plugins\KeeperSpawner\KeeperSpawner.GK2Framework.dll[/code]
[*]Optional: install GK2 Mod Framework as described on its page.
[*]Load a save and press [b]O[/b].
[/list]
[i]KeeperSpawner.GK2Framework.dll[/i] is the small bridge to GK2 Mod Framework. Without the Framework, BepInEx skips it with a "missing dependencies" line in the log; that is expected.

Updating from 1.0.0: extract the new zip over the old files. Your settings, favorites and recent items are kept.

Uninstall: delete the [i]BepInEx\plugins\KeeperSpawner[/i] folder.

Also on the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3810736028]Steam Workshop[/url] (needs the GK2 Workshop Loader). Do not install it both from the Workshop and manually.

[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]O[/b]: open / close (configurable)
[*][b]Click[/b]: add the amount selected under "Click" (1 / 10 / Max)
[*][b]Shift+Click[/b]: add 1
[*][b]Right-click[/b]: add / remove favorite
[*][b]Ctrl+F[/b]: search
[*][b]Esc[/b]: leave the search box, then close
[/list]

[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
In game: [b]Mods > KeeperSpawner > Settings[/b] (with GK2 Mod Framework): hotkey, amount per click, quest items, view, UI scale, background dimming.
Or edit [i]BepInEx\config\com.mrkacmaz.keeperspawner.cfg[/i] (created on the first start).

[size=5][b]Nothing happens when I press O?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Load a save first. The window does not open in the main menu.
[*]The key is the letter [b]O[/b], not the number zero.
[*]Open [i]Graveyard Keeper 2\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] and look for [i]KeeperSpawner 1.1.0 loaded[/i]. If the line is missing, BepInEx did not load the mod: check that [i]BepInEx\plugins\KeeperSpawner\KeeperSpawner.dll[/i] exists and that BepInEx itself starts.
[*][i]KeeperSpawner disabled: ...[/i] in the log means a game update changed something the mod needs. Please report it with the log.
[*]Missing from the Mods menu? Both DLLs must be in the same folder, and you need GK2 Mod Framework 0.1.19 or newer. The log should contain [i]Registered GK2 mod [com.mrkacmaz.keeperspawner][/i].
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Tested with game version 1.007.1 (Steam build 25601286) and GK2 Mod Framework 0.1.19.
[*]Items are added with the same call the game's own scripts use, so they stay in your save. Keeping a backup of your save is still a good idea.
[*]The mod does not use the network, does not delete files and does not load other code.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Bug reports and source[/b][/size]
Report bugs in the Bugs tab or on [url=https://github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner/issues/new/choose]GitHub[/url], with [i]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] attached.
Source code: [url=https://github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner]github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner[/url] (MIT).
